@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Follow external file-open requests
+
+This local extension lets a host reuse a dedicated Files pane when a user clicks
+another path in an agent terminal. The host resolves relative paths using the
+source terminal's directory before handing them to the viewer.
+
+## Contract
+
+- Opt in with `HERDR_FILE_VIEWER_REQUEST_FILE=/absolute/path/request.json`.
+- Atomically replace that file with `{"id":"unique-request-id","target":"docs/plan.md"}`.
+  `target` accepts the same file/line/range grammar as `--open`.
+- The viewer only reads the request file. It does not create a service, execute
+  commands from requests, or write the viewed files.
+- Requests are bound to the startup tree root. Out-of-root paths remain rejected
+  by the existing open-target resolver. A host uses a different dedicated viewer
+  for a different root.
+- Only a new ID changes the selection. While a modal is open, the newest request
+  waits; closing the modal applies it without discarding the input.
+- Within-root navigation preserves annotations and pins. Manually opened Files
+  panes without the request-file variable are unaffected.
+- An accepted request shows the file content across the preview pane, including
+  narrow splits. Press `z` to reveal the file tree when desired.
+- Reads are bounded to 16 KiB and polled every 250 ms. Missing, oversized,
+  malformed and non-regular files leave the current preview intact.
+
+## Readiness and verification
+
+The feature uses the existing `apply_open_target` seam and renderer worker.
+Tests cover root ownership, modal ownership and deduplication. Host integration
+is verified with actual Ctrl-click input, absolute/relative Markdown paths,
+Unicode, spaces, wrapped paths, repeated-open process identity and the source
+terminal remaining alive.
